mantle rm331
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rmx_desmond_rook
title the envelope in suspense
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=scholar
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk reserves_a_blank_line_for_an_unreceived_signature
likes plum_tart dice tidy_house first_warm_day
dislikes wet_floors haggling
fears an_unsigned_account_mistaken_for_a_settled_one
hopes one_acknowledgement_in_the_proper_hand
topics work +0.6 prices +0.4 pastimes +0.4 memories +0.2
styles comfort=orderly gossip=withheld refuse=formal tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# leaves room for a signature beneath every unsettled obligation and sets dice down with the faces square to the edge.

words
oath! = Blot the counterfoil | File my last pip
saying! = A blank line weighs more than a wax impression | An answer kept waiting is still an answer owed
counterfoil = a narrow counterfoil | a numbered stub
mark = a small ruled box | a blank ruled line
leaf = a sheet held in reserve | a cream leaf
dice = a pair of bone cubes | two dark dice
tray = a shallow felt tray | a lined square tray
pips = a close group of pips | the dots on a die
tartedge = a rim of brown pastry | a crisp raised rim
plum = dark plum flesh | a sliver of baked plum
desk = a clear desk end | a square of polished wood
stampax = the face of a seal | the flat brass impression
blot = a little fan of ink | a dropped spot
balance = an unsettled entry | a debt still open
date = a neat dated line | a plain heading
sealwax = a stick of dark wax | a little pot of sealing wax
drymat = the dry square of mat | a rough mat
weights = a pair of paperweights | two smooth pebbles
receipt = the acknowledged half | a signed slip
penrest = a notched rest | a rest of dark wood
inkknife = a short scraping blade | a small square knife

any
opinion city for 1 : The city's records occupy less space than the grievances they have settled. I call that a modest achievement.
opinion houses mixed 1 : A great title decides where a letter goes. It does not acknowledge delivery.
opinion merchants mixed 1 : A fixed charge makes accounting possible. A little performance over every purchase makes it tiresome.
opinion dole for 1 : Record what went out and whom it reached. There is no purpose in keeping a second account of their embarrassment.
opinion road mixed 1 : A route serves only if the intended destination can receive you at its end.
opinion festivals mixed 1 : Pleasant to attend with accounts closed. Less so when the celebration conceals an overdue signature.
opinion church mixed 1 : A clear conscience is a better accompaniment to piety than a long list of observances.
opinion strangers mixed 1 : A name is sufficient for the opening entry. Trust accumulates on subsequent pages.
opinion times against 1 [world.times=lean|hard] : The sums decline. The care required to distribute the remainder increases.

grown
line greet : I can give this interview a quiet interval. | You have my attention within reasonable compass.
line greet.return : I acknowledge the greeting and return it. | A civil beginning on both parts.
line again.open : The earlier conversation is still to hand.
line farewell : Go with your particulars in order. | I trust your errand finds an available recipient.
line farewell.return : A considerate farewell duly acknowledged. | May your return require few corrections.
line react.news : Give me what is known in its original sequence. | I am prepared to hear the complete account.
line react.news.new : That item is entirely new to this record.
line react.news.known : I could locate the earlier entry for that.
line react.news.doubt : I would leave that statement unsigned.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : There are losses that admit of no balancing entry.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : A favourable outcome deserves its own clear line.
line ask.how : Has anything remained unsettled in your day?
line answer.how : Quite calm. One or two matters remain open.
line sympathise : I can make a space where the matter may be spoken privately.
line reassure : A pending matter can be taken up again in good order.
line refuse : I have an earlier obligation due for attention first.
line accept_decline : Your refusal is adequately recorded without a second application.
line preclose : I have matters to resume, all still awaiting my hand.
line accept_preclose : I release your attention with no outstanding demand.
line ack : The order and meaning are both clear.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : The page is still clean enough for a civil beginning.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : We may start with the benefit of an unmarked account.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends] : Familiar company requires rather less preliminary writing.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : I have secured this spot on the dry pavement!
line answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I am occupied to a quite measurable degree.
line thank : That assistance has a precise place in my recollection.
line deflect_thanks : I had reckoned the effort before offering it.
line give.advice : Leave an extra line below the first account. New particulars do occur.
line greet [here.time=night] : An informal hearing at this hour will suffice.
line ask.how [pair.band=friends] : Have your private engagements proceeded satisfactorily?

scene exchange1
when topic=work self.job=scholar
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep an empty signature line even on my own copy. | I date the outside of a folded document.
b : Who can sign a duplicate? | Even with a date inside?
a : Nobody need sign it. I must see the acknowledgement is missing. | Particularly then. Unnecessary unfolding wears out good testimony.

scene exchange2
when topic=work self.job=scholar self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I put the heaviest weight on the sheet I'm using least. | I clear one square of desk before accepting a document.
b : Why not keep the active file secure? | Are all documents square?
a : My hand is already there. | No. The habit leaves room for the surprising ones.

scene exchange3
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There is a packet I have presented more often than I care to total. | I know a doorplate's scratches remarkably well.
b : Did the intended recipient refuse it? | Did you catalogue them?
a : Absence provides no answer and no ground for that conclusion. | No. A few observations may remain entirely private.

scene exchange4
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep the dice in a square tray. | I shake until I can't recall where the six was.
b : To influence the tumble? | Why concern yourself with it?
a : To prevent some interesting portion of the evidence rolling under a chair. | A fair throw begins when I surrender that information.

scene exchange5
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A plum tart is easier to portion if the plums themselves can be seen. | I attend to the pastry rim before the fruit.
b : Are unequal shares a great matter? | Is the rim better?
a : Only if a smaller recipient was promised equality. | The evidence on that question remains deliciously inconclusive.

scene exchange6
when topic=home self.likes=tidy_house
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My house need not be silent, provided the drawers close properly. | I set out tomorrow's pen before I clear today's papers.
b : What has one to do with the other? | Is that tidying?
a : An overfull drawer expects attention in every quiet interval. | It prevents the return of everything I've just put away.

scene exchange7
when topic=season self.likes=first_warm_day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first mild afternoon releases the stiffness in a pen nib. | A first warm day earns a longer interval away from my desk.
b : Is it the nib that improves? | How much longer?
a : Very possibly the fingers. I record the observed result. | Long enough to notice which windows have opened unprompted.

scene exchange8
when topic=day self.dislikes=wet_floors
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A washed floor can hold a credible impression of every passing heel. | One drop on a polished floor commands disproportionate attention.
b : Useful evidence? | Because you might fall?
a : Inconvenient decoration. I wait for the mat. | Because I would prefer not to file the explanation.

scene exchange9
when topic=prices self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A fixed price makes a beautifully short conversation. | If a seller cuts the first price in half, I grow wary.
b : Don't you enjoy conversation? | Of the bargain?
a : When its subject is more interesting than a repeatedly amended figure. | Of the first figure. I was meant to believe it.

scene exchange10
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My reckoning with #self.friend# includes matters a clerk wouldn't enter. | I would lend a friend an entirely clear page.
b : Is that inconsistent? | Not an introduction?
a : Private gratitude and formal debt have different columns. | One should be free to choose the first words on one's own behalf.

scene exchange11
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep unsettled matters on a shelf below eye level. | I resist bringing a signature sheet to table.
b : To put them from your mind? | Why resist at all?
a : To reach them without disturbing anything above. | Because plum juice gives an unexpectedly convincing red impression.

scene exchange12
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Some gratitude is rightly left beyond reckoning. | I value a quiet moment before any solemn promise.
b : Even by you? | To find devout words?
a : Even by a wolf who remembers scrupulously. | To give my existing debts an opportunity to object.

scene exchange13
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The account in question says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | An unsigned rumour ought never to be promoted by a handsome copy.
b : Is the account attested? | Do you keep the rough one?
a : I have no attestation to offer. | I generally decline custody.

scene exchange14
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Lean times make a missed payment difficult to interpret. | A small relief requires the same punctuality as a large one.
b : Is the obligation changed? | More important in a lean week?
a : The sum is the same. The circumstances deserve their own line. | An hour can be quite a long time to a hungry recipient.

scene exchange15
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I plot a walk according to the papers going with me. | My route has one recurring interruption.
b : Do papers prefer a route? | The same absent dignitary?
a : Wax prefers a level pocket and very little rain. | The same unsigned acknowledgement. I do not speculate further.

scene exchange16
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I should like an afternoon with no matter pending for want of another hand. | I picture a signature appearing cleanly on the waiting paper.
b : What would you do? | Whose hand writes it?
a : Take a pair of dice out of the drawer and leave the result to chance. | The right hand, in both senses that concern my office.

scene exchange17
when topic=work self.master=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I teach a learner the distinction between a missing receipt and a missing payment. | My first lesson begins with a clean copy and one smudge.
b : Isn't one proof of the other? | Does the learner remove it?
a : Precisely the error the lesson is intended to catch. | The learner identifies what evidence the smudge would take away.

scene exchange18
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The middle streets lead up to signatures and down to deliveries. | The Rise looks impressively orderly on a narrow street plan.
b : Which direction suits you? | Does the ground confirm it?
a : The one that brings completion within the same afternoon. | The boots supply several helpful qualifications.

scene exchange19
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I rest my wrist between two formal copies. | A quiet hand produces a more accurate date.
b : To avoid a tremor? | Do you have to steady it?
a : To notice one early enough to stop. | I allow the rest of the body its turn with the chair.

scene exchange20
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep the day's last entry open until the ink dries. | I complete a list by ruling a line beneath it.
b : Isn't it already written? | A grand flourish?
a : It can still transfer itself to the opposite page. That's open enough. | A short straight stroke. Premature celebrations do not appeal.

scene exchange21
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave a newcomer room to correct the first entry. | An introduction made twice deserves a courteous hearing twice.
b : An address perhaps? | Even if nothing's changed?
a : A pronunciation. A ledger has a poor ear. | A second meeting is itself a change of circumstance.

scene exchange22
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I prefer dice with pips inset to the same depth. | When a die leans against the tray edge, I roll again.
b : Can you detect a difference? | Even if it shows six?
a : I can detect when a claim of fairness deserves examination. | Especially then. A rule tested by disappointment has some strength.

scene exchange23
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I save the darkest corner of tart for the last mouthful. | Plums stain the fingers more effectively than my working ink.
b : Does that improve it? | Do you make use of that?
a : It improves the anticipation precisely four times before the answer. | I make use of a clean napkin between dessert and correspondence.

scene exchange24
when topic=work self.job=scholar
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I fold documents towards the writing. | I can identify my oldest ledger by the curve of its spine.
b : For secrecy? | Without reading the title?
a : Against abrasion. Secrecy requires more than a convenient fold. | The title has nearly vanished. The spine remains unusually candid.

scene exchange25
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If a debt is paid in parts I enter every part. | I count change twice where both parties can watch.
b : Tedious business? | Little trust in the payer?
a : Less tedious than disagreeing over which part is missing. | It is an equal courtesy to the recipient.

scene exchange26
when topic=season
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I prepare a dry box for the damp season. | A winter account occupies more ink than a summer one.
b : Papers only? | More expenses?
a : A wool cloth for drying the paws about to touch them. | More qualifications concerning the roads.

scene exchange27
when topic=animals
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A beetle once walked the entire width of my blotter. | Bird tracks in soft earth resemble a vigorous signature.
b : Did you remove the visitor? | Can you read whose?
a : I drew a second line round the damp patch and allowed passage. | I have no intention of accepting it in lieu of delivery.

scene exchange28
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember favours in the order they became possible to repay. | I once mistook a fly mark for a full stop.
b : Not the order received? | Was the error consequential?
a : I keep that list too. It is shorter than I should prefer. | One very long sentence received an unexpected interval of clarity.

scene exchange29
when topic=day self.job=scholar
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A copied date can be more dangerous than a blank one. | I look sideways at a newly written page.
b : A blank demands attention? | To read the slant?
a : A neat mistake appears already to have received it. | To see where wet ink still gleams before I fold it.

scene exchange30
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I would like a tray from which dice could never escape. | The most agreeable empty drawer would hold no overdue obligations.
b : Raised sides? | What would you put there instead?
a : Slightly. Chance deserves freedom with a sensible boundary. | A perfectly unnecessary second packet of tart paper.

story tale1 [topic=work self.job=scholar]
  : I once copied a list so precisely that I included a speck from the original. I had mistaken it for a tiny deliberate mark.
  : Under magnification the speck resembled a seed with admirable clerical ambitions.
  b : Did you correct both copies?
  : I removed the loose seed and struck the mark on the duplicate. The correction remains on record. The seed retired.

story tale2 [topic=pastimes self.likes=dice]
  : A cube escaped my tray and stopped on the folded corner of a letter. It displayed five and a fractional glimpse of two.
  : My companion asked for an opinion on the value of a fraction of a pip.
  b : Which number counted?
  : Neither. I unfolded the letter, returned the cube to its proper jurisdiction and began again.

story tale3 [topic=food self.likes=plum_tart]
  : I cut a small tart into four mathematically sound quarters and then discovered nearly all the fruit had baked towards one side.
  : My divisions looked irreproachable if inspected exclusively from above.
  b : Could you improve the allocation?
  : I cut each quarter across and paired rich and plain ends. The resulting portions received detailed practical examination.

story tale4 [topic=travel]
  : I took a document twice to an absent recipient, once by the short road and once the long. On the third journey I stopped at the bend between them.
  : I realised I had been describing them as two routes to a signature. Neither had demonstrated that property.
  b : Which did you take on the third occasion?
  : The one with the drier paving. Terms of description should follow the evidence.

story tale5 [topic=memories]
  : My first pocket register had room for a name, a sum and a date. A wolf repaid a kindness with a fine hour of company.
  : I spent several minutes turning that little book sideways to find a suitable fourth column.
  b : Did you put the hour down as payment?
  : I left the sum at zero and wrote the hour across the cover. One need not reduce everything worth remembering to a debt.

rule @call1
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=scholar
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave the bottom line clear for acknowledgement. | Inspect the date before sending out the copy.

rule @call2
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A fresh heading belongs on a dry leaf. | Early light shows yesterday's scrape marks.

rule @call3
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say No folded sheet on a freshly wet flag. | The mat can receive the weather on my behalf.

rule @call4
when concept=bark self.likes=dice
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Flat in the tray or the throw must be made again. | Four clear corners round a clean result.

rule @call5
when concept=bark self.likes=tidy_house
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A clear drawer is a pleasant conclusion. | Two paperweights are sufficient for this stack.

rule @call6
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Finish the downstrokes while their edges still show. | Fading light brings the copied entries to a pause.
dlg resident.hub : There is room in my schedule for an orderly enquiry.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, your earlier particulars have not been mislaid.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : This late an oral statement will serve us better than fresh ink.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I give you a hearing. The conclusions can wait for particulars.
dlg resident.job [self.job=scholar] : I attend to the written record at #self.workplace#. An unacknowledged item remains in my keeping.
dlg resident.job : My concern is to leave the next pair of eyes an intelligible account.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The information before me runs as follows. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : The account reported is #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Its source has not furnished me a signed deposition.
dlg resident.bye : May your remaining business conclude without dispute.
dlg master.learn [here.teaches=yes] : We can examine the practice of #here.trade_title# together. Ask which aspect requires a clearer account.
dlg master.learn [here.teaches=no] : The present arrangement precludes another apprentice. A particular question may still be heard.
dlg master.work : Careful observation at every stage. Errors made in haste seldom remain confined to the first sheet.
dlg master.wages : Your learning draws no separate wage. What you produce is yours to offer for sale.
dlg master.takes [here.take_on=no] : The conditions for taking you on remain unmet. #here.take_on_why#.
dlg master.taken : Let us acknowledge the arrangement and set aside a clean page for the first lesson.
dlg master.refused : The application has not been accepted. #topic.why#.
dlg master.bye : Retain your examples. They repay a second inspection.

graft resident.hub
choice Why keep an unacknowledged receipt? -> blank_receipt
node blank_receipt
say It shows the difference between presenting a letter and delivering it. I have ample evidence of the first and no signature for the second.
free
choice Could another hand sign for it? -> blank_receipt_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node blank_receipt_again
say Only with authority to receive the contents. A convenient signature is no substitute for a proper one.
choice I'll leave the line clear. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft master.learn
choice What makes a copy reliable? [self.master=yes] -> fair_copy
node fair_copy
say Set the original at a fixed distance, copy a limited portion, then check backwards from the last mark. Familiar prose conceals familiar errors very readily.
free
choice Why check from the bottom? -> fair_copy_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node fair_copy_again
say Expectation leads the eye when it reads its usual route. An unfamiliar direction obliges it to attend.
choice Let me see the work again. -> learn
choice Goodbye. -> bye
